:false,"_score_spread":27.3,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.548320395740225,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":8.6,"_gate_incr_roic":-0.046054767249226615,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":1.3,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":-0.0575906373450763,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.11920705196466785,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.035542045153324375,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":5.6,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.12742,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":84.9,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Ladder Capital Corp operates as an internally-managed real estate investment trust in the United States. It operates through three segments: Loans, Securities, and Real Estate. The Loans segment originates and acquires balance sheet loans that provide interim financing to borrowers seeking short-term capital for the acquisition or transition of commercial real estate; originates conduit loans, which are first mortgage loans on commercial real estate properties for sale in commercial mortgage-backed securities securitizations; and invests in note purchase financings, subordinated debt, mezzanine debt, and other structured finance products related to commercial real estate. Its Securities segment invests in CMBS, U.S. Agency securities, corporate bonds, equity securities, and U.S. Treasury securities that are not classified as cash and cash equivalents. The Real Estate segment engages in net leased properties, other diversified real estate, and investments in unconsolidated ventures. The company qualifies as a real estate investment trust for federal income tax purposes. It generally would not be subject to federal corporate income taxes if it distributes at least 90% of its taxable income to its stockholders. Ladder Capital Corp was founded in 2008 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Brian Richard Harris | Founder, CEO & Director | Age 65 | Compensation: $5.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 60 people. Each employee generates $1.3M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $339K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Ladder Capital Corp is a small-cap real estate business with a $1.1B market cap.","The top line has compounded at +10% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are expanding by +7.2pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 14% against a 8% cost of capital, a 5-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $79M in free cash flow, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.37\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 11.9% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 13% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Real Estate peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 70% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","11 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Real Estate peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Among the least levered in Real Estate \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Trading Systems Reacting to (LADR) Volatility","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/17/Trading_Systems_Reacting_to_LADR_Volatility_111226074002_1794487202.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794487202.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Sunrise Realty Trust (NASDAQ:SUNS) versus Ladder Capital (NYSE:LADR) Head to Head Comparison","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/sunrise-realty-trust-nasdaqsuns-versus-ladder-capital-nyseladr-head-to-head-comparison.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794484018.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.949,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Head to Head Review: Starwood Property Trust (NYSE:STWD) & Ladder Capital (NYSE:LADR)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/08/head-to-head-review-starwood-property-trust-nysestwd-ladder-capital-nyseladr.html","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794149933.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.96,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What Ladder Capital (LADR)'s Real Estate Gain Means For Shareholders","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nyse-ladr/ladder-capital/news/what-ladder-capital-ladrs-real-estate-gain-means-for-shareho","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793964546.685,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.935,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Blackstone Mortgage Trust (NYSE:BXMT) versus Ladder Capital (NYSE:LADR) Head to Head Contrast","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/blackstone-mortgage-trust-nysebxmt-versus-ladder-capital-nyseladr-head-to-head-contrast.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":179379